From d1a1be824576284c41a2915e040ee5d3b4b459ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:30:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sync): attribute selection probes and checkpoint proof
 CPU [daveey]

Problem: run16 live non-board CPU remains 11.798 ms/round; select is 2.925 ms/round while wait fell to 1.009. The global checkpoint-keep counter cannot identify its triggering step or proof subpart. Why the remaining selection cost is high is not established; changing restore defenses from fixture timings would repeat the failed sizing assumption.

Add inclusive sync.detail diagnostics for executed select outbox probes and checkpoint WAL/shrink/schema work, plus checkpoint keeps by triggering step. Preserve all selection short circuits and restore predicates. These records use outer=False, never create sync.step or sync.board entries, and do not change total-minus-board accounting. Instrumentation is diagnostic, not a claimed performance cut or live acceptance.

Proof: three behavioral tests fail on parent due to absent counters, pass on candidate. Six exact-anchor instrumentation mutants killed by named tests; 15 importer test files pass (285 tests); scripts/check passes. Restore guard and existing tests unchanged. Independent review must explicitly check restore-safety preservation and nonadditive accounting. No Mac actions; natural deployment and a new valid live window remain required.
